# tools/l/living_pin_near_bound_witness.rish -- the pin advisory reads the set the law names.
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/l/living_pin_near_bound_witness.rish
#
# WHY. The pin law seats one roster and one bound reading so that two roofs cannot disagree about
# which pages are pins or about how heavy a pin may be. Duty 6 of the docs lint kept the bound
# reading -- tools/fixtures/l/living_pin_max_bytes.sh, one home since REDS %199 -- and walked a
# docs roster of its own, so four of the seven pins seated in
# tools/fixtures/l/living_pin_guard_roster.txt were never weighed by it: EQUINOX_SEAT_MAP, REDS,
# SHRED_PREP and prin_scope. Measured on 20260831, duty 6 advised on glow/README.md and
# construction/ITINERARY.md and said nothing about construction/REDS.md at 24,555 of 24,576 or
# construction/SHRED_PREP.md at 24,366 -- 99.9% and 99.1% of their bounds. The pin it could not see
# had shipped 1,040 bytes over that same morning (REDS %395), and the guard that would have caught
# the overage weighs only the pins a commit stages, which a rebase never does.
#
# THE SECOND FAULT, in the same duty. The near list hung off an `elif` below the past-bound list, so
# it printed only while nothing was over. The one moment a reader most wants to know which pins are
# about to follow is the moment one of them has already crossed, and that is precisely the moment
# the elder form went quiet.
#
# WHAT THIS PROVES, and where. The control builds real trees in a throwaway pen and reads what duty
# 6 says about each: a seated pin absent from the docs roster is named, the same pen with the union
# line reverted says nothing about it, a docs page absent from the seated roster is still named, a
# near pin prints beside a past-bound one, the same pen with the near list hung back off the over
# list goes silent, a page carrying its own bound is advised against ITS number, that same page
# comfortably under its own bound says nothing, and a path standing on both rosters is weighed once.
# Five of the ten bite against the departing scan, which is what tells a repair from a rewording.
#
# AND THE PEN STATES ITS OWN PRECONDITION. Case 0 asserts that the three planted sizes still land in
# the bands their case labels claim -- near, over, comfortably under -- each computed from the law
# through the same fixture the duty reads. The sizes were spelled as absolutes until 20260906, when
# the law seated living_pin_max_bytes[construction/REDS.md] at 40,960 and a 24,000-byte plant went
# from 97.6% of that page's bound to 58.6% of it. Three cases failed and none of them said why: a
# pen that plants an absolute is testing a snapshot of the law, and a pen that plants a ratio is
# testing the law.
#
# WHAT IT DOES NOT REACH. The live tree's own reading, which tools/l/living_docs_lint.rish already
# prints on every roster pass at a cost of 55 seconds -- paying for it twice would buy nothing. And
# whether a page NEAR its bound should be folded, condensed, or left alone, which is a hand's
# judgement about meaning rather than a number.
#
# WHY IT IS ITS OWN GUARD rather than an assertion inside the lint. living_docs_lint is a ratchet
# advisory that never fails by design, so a check placed there could not red -- and a guard that
# cannot red guards nothing.
#
# Pen: tools/fixtures/l/living_pin_near_bound_control.sh -- ten behaviors, both faults shown from
# the side where the reading goes silent. Run from the repository root.

say "living-pin-near-bound: Language EN -- a pin advisory is worth exactly the set of pins it weighs."
say "living-pin-near-bound: Style Gauge, Meter -- every count below is the control's own output."
say "living-pin-near-bound: Lens TAME -- say why: the union is the law's own roster joined to the docs roster, so the reading covers the set the law names rather than the set this duty happened to hold."

let control = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/l/living_pin_near_bound_control.sh"]
say control.out
assert control.ok else "living-pin-near-bound: the control must complete"
assert control.out contains "control_checks=10" else "living-pin-near-bound: all ten behaviors must be read"
assert control.out contains "control_failures=0" else "living-pin-near-bound: every planted behavior must read as written"
assert control.out contains "control_verdict=ok" else "living-pin-near-bound: the control must agree with itself"

assert control.out contains "plants_agree_with_law=yes" else "living-pin-near-bound: the planted sizes must still land in the bands their cases name, read from the law rather than spelled"
assert control.out contains "seated_pin_named=yes" else "living-pin-near-bound: a pin the law seats must be weighed even when the docs roster lacks it"
assert control.out contains "seated_pin_silent_without_union=no" else "living-pin-near-bound: reverting the union must silence that reading, or the union carries nothing"
assert control.out contains "docs_page_still_named=yes" else "living-pin-near-bound: the union must add without taking away"
assert control.out contains "over_bound_named=yes" else "living-pin-near-bound: a pin past its bound must be named"
assert control.out contains "near_printed_beside_over=yes" else "living-pin-near-bound: the near list must print beside the past-bound list"
assert control.out contains "near_silent_when_hung_off_over=no" else "living-pin-near-bound: hanging the near list off the over list must silence it, or the split carries nothing"
assert control.out contains "own_bound_in_message=yes" else "living-pin-near-bound: a page carrying its own bound must be advised against ITS number"
assert control.out contains "own_bound_page_silent=no" else "living-pin-near-bound: a page far under its own bound must say nothing"
assert control.out contains "union_dedupes=yes" else "living-pin-near-bound: a path on both rosters must be weighed once"

say ""
say "GREEN: living-pin-near-bound -- duty 6 weighs the docs roster joined to the seated pin roster, advises each page against its own bound with its headroom named, and prints the near list beside the past-bound one; ten behaviors proven in a throwaway pen, its plants sized from the law rather than spelled, both faults shown from the silent side."
